{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1103247-demon-fallen-rome-setting","id":1103247,"title":"[Demon] Fallen Rome Setting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-13T13:18:43-07:00","id":1103247,"title":"[Demon] Fallen Rome Setting","content":"I just found an old file on my PC that's essentially the basis for the setting I made up for a game set in Rome I ran...what, seven years ago? It's old. Anyways, back then I created an entire setting, filled with NPCs for all factions, sides and houses, wrote the storyline for a game that could have lasted for years and even had ideas for what the Fallen society was for all the bigger Italian cities. A complete setting that proved useless since that particular game only lasted 8 sessions. Meh, we all know how these things go sometimes.<br /> <br /> Still, I do think I had some good ideas back then and that posting something that's already written can't hurt, if it has the potential to give others some ideas. I do still have the notes for the whole setting but actually managed to sit down and write only the introduction. When the game ended, I was not in the mood to keep going. It's a bit campy, because my younger self had the brilliant idea to go for the tone of some books, resulting in my own clumsy attempt to replicate the CWoD's setting book style. Another one for the &quot;things you did when you were younger that now make you facepalm&quot; list. Anyways, here it is. If you are interested for more, I can always share my other notes.<br /> <br /> <i><b>From the words of Michele Manfredi, also known as Eligos, demonic herald of the Fourth House:</b></i><br /> <br /> <i>So, I understand you were asking around for someone able to give you a decent overview of the city and they sent you to me, right? Fine. I suppose that when your main hobby is keeping an eye on everybody, you're bound to develop a reputation. Hey, don't judge me: I'm a knowledge gatherer. I was one before the fall, I tried to be one while in the Abyss and I'm still one even after merging with a human. My job is to learn secrets. Doesn't mean I'll share them, though. Well, at least not the juicy ones, but I don't see anything wrong in a little informal chat...</i><br /> <br /> <i>Rome. Believe me when I say that, as a Fallen, few cities can rival the opportunities offered by the Eternal City. Yeah, I've heard all those stories about Los Angeles; everybody has. Forgive me if I say that I couldn't care less. From the moment you've slipped through the cracks of the Abyss, Rome can give you every thing you'll will ever need. Money, power, knowledge, an enormous amount of pure, unbridled Faith: it's all out there, if you're strong enough to take it. It's not easy, mind you: great opportunities bring even greater risks</i><br /> <br /> <i>Rome's a battleground, and not all the sides fighting for dominance are part of the Fallen Host. There are things buried beneath the ruins and most are best left untouched. Something really bad happened here during ancient times and I suspect we still have to face some of its consequences. I have my theories on this matter; perhaps I'll share them with you later.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Faith flows through the city like a river. I'm not kidding: even outside the Vatican City, there are places where you can almost feel it on your skin. It both means that it's far too easy to exploit it and to suffer its burning caress. All this Faith is inevitably tied to the Catholic Church, which, although not the only one, certainly represents the area's main source of belief. Rome and the Catholic faith have been entwined for thousands of years, ranging from Nero's persecutions, passing trough Constantine and the hundreds of Popes who lived here.<br /> <br /> The number of Fallen around here is impressive even for a city of this size, and it grows every day. Each new Fallen is promptly enrolled in the not-so-cold war between the various Factions and gains a dozens of enemies without even knowing them. Add the usual petty rivalries for territory and resources, not to mention ancient grudges from before our imprisonment, and you'll understand why the competition around here is so...intense. I was already in Rome before the creation of a formal Infernal Court, and I can tell you things were even worse then: all the Factions stubbornly refused to discuss or come at terms with the others, and trivial discussions often escalated in violent conflicts. It was a real mess, thrust me, but we're still creatures of order (even if its <i>our</i> order), and, as soon the population grew enough and some decent leaders emerged from the various groups, we organized ourselves-</i><br /> <br /> <i>In order to reach a compromise between the factions, though, we had to make a few adjustements to the classical model of Infernal Court. Nobody, and I mean <i>nobody</i>, was willing to let a Demon of another faction to become the Tyrant of Rome. They simply could not care less about how close you were to the Lightbringer during the War or if you spit in Michael's eyes before being sent into the Abyss; back then, the title of Tyrant simply was not going to be assigned . The Factions had too much to loose and handing the keys of Rome to a single individual was not part of their plans. Today, we say that the Tyrant's seat is &quot;vacant&quot;, while two Consuls are elected yearly in order to govern the city. During the year they're in charge, the Consuls are the highest power in town, but they can pose a veto to each other's decisions. We still have the five Ministries, but the usual council of ministers is now part of our personal answer to the Senate of Ancient Rome. Each Pentarch is the formal leader of his ministry, but the organization itself is represented by a total of seven Fallen. The Pentarch selects the others six and, while the Consuls may easily nominate or dismiss the ministers or the other members of the Senate, such practice is usually frowned upon (unless the Senator deserved it, of course). Five Ministries with seven Senators each, plus two Consuls: that's the official ruling body of Rome's Infernal Court, also known as the Marble Court. Technically speaking, the current Court is only waiting the coming of a Demon &quot;unequivocally worthy of the title of Tyrant and uncontested leader of the Roman Fallen&quot;, but, personally, I doubt that's going to happen without much trouble. Treachery and backstabbings abound, it's not clear wheteher the loyalties of Consuls and Senators lie within the court, their respective Factions or themselves, but the Marble Court's existence is preferable to the alternative and, to its credit, it usually manages to provide the various Fallens a way to discuss the problems of the city along with all kind of requests from the demonic population (having political weight still helps, though)</i><br /> <br /> <i>It goes without saying that a lot of Demons are not satisfied by the current state of things. Within the upper echelons of the Fallen's society, there are plenty of aspirant Tyrants. The leaders of the Faction are those who look after that position the most. Sure, you may pull some strings and have one of yours elected this year, but that's not even comparable to the lasting absolute authority of a true Tyrant. I think we should be really careful if we ever see one of the Faction's heads elected as Consul: it means that he's confident enough he'll be able to pull a Julius Caesar and seize all the power. Here's my two cents about that: if you ever have the chance to do so, don't take that risk. Once you're up there, it's easy to forget how things ended up for the real Caesar. </i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T14:28:02-07:00","id":1103621,"title":"","content":"Dude...i been dming Demon for years and i read that and...I cant stop touching myself (read it as a : I love it)<br /> <br /> I wsa thinking with a demon seting for the ancient mesopotiamia/babylon empire but this is neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T06:59:18-07:00","id":1104265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1103247-demon-fallen-rome-setting?p=1103621#post1103621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude...i been dming Demon for years and i read that and...I cant stop touching myself (read it as a : I love it)<br /> <br /> I wsa thinking with a demon seting for the ancient mesopotiamia/babylon empire but this is neat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Glad you liked it.<br /> <br /> Long story short, the plan for the factions was for the Reconcilers to be the single strongest faction, with a cardinal as the quite aggressive leader and having meetings in places where High-Torment Demon would burst into flames, Raveners being the weakest but managing to survive because of a couple of powerful high-rank demons acting as deterrent, Cryptics having a lot of things to study about in Rome and Luciferans and Faustian being the middle ground, with the Faustian focusing more on the mundane side of things (political and economical power) and the Luciferans being numerous but lacking leadership.<br /> <br /> Plus quite a lot of Earthbounds and the consequences of their actions in the Ancient Rome. The less original one was one sleeping under the Colosseum","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T09:16:58-07:00","id":1106087,"title":"","content":"Interesting!<br /> <br /> Are there any Earthbound in Rome, in your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-21T09:22:16-07:00","id":1106092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1103247-demon-fallen-rome-setting?p=1106087#post1106087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting!<br /> <br /> Are there any Earthbound in Rome, in your games?</div> </div> </div> </div>The plan was to have plenty. Both survivors from Ancient Rome and new ones. An idea I wanted to keep there was that the Fallen took control of Rome without knowing how bad the Earthbound situation there was, something that would eventually come up in the game.<br /> <br /> As for the wider picture, there's a big Earthbound under the Vesuvius and Etna"